Threshold N: freeze reported at 3000ms. Pick threshold 5s? AC says "> N sec". I'll make default `Duration(seconds: 5)`? Hmm, but on a slow iOS cold start 3s to first frame might be normal-ish. Reported freeze at 3000ms uptime. If threshold is 5s, we'd never breadcrumb a 3s freeze. But uptime 3000ms is when feedback was submitted, "freeze ~3s after launch". Choose threshold 3s? That could false-positive on slow devices. I'll go with 4s default... Actually, let me make it configurable via dart-define `FA_BOOT_WATCHDOG_MS` with default 5000? Hmm.

Let me think about what's most useful: the point is the NEXT TestFlight feedback should be actionable. A breadcrumb at >5s is fine — a true hang has no upper bound. The reported freeze is 3s+ though. I'll default to 4 seconds. Hmm, hard to know cold-start p95 on iPhone 15 Pro. iPhone 15 Pro is fast; 4s to first frame would definitely be anomalous there. Go with 4s, configurable via `--dart-define=FA_BOOT_WATCHDOG_MS`.

